# Local-only project notes.
AGENTS.md

# Simulator output. tb_zc_seq.v dumps zc.vcd on every run, so without this the
# working tree is dirty after each regression pass.
*.vcd
*.vvp
a.out

# SD-card bring-up artifacts. *.bin is broad but safe here: the only .bin files
# this project ever produces are qpsk.bin and frame.bin, both regenerable with
# `python3 fpga/check_frame.py gen`.
*.bin

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vivado
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything under ofdm_bd/ is generated by fpga/build_bd.tcl and is fully
# reproducible with:
#     vivado -mode batch -source fpga/build_bd.tcl
# The source of truth is that script plus the RTL it references. The generated
# project is worth ignoring because:
#   - the run trees are tens of MB and churn on every build, which bloats
#     history permanently (git history cannot be cleaned without a rewrite),
#   - they embed absolute paths from the machine that built them (e.g.
#     C:/Users/adira/...), so they are not portable and leak the username,
#   - they carry no information the script does not already have.
/ofdm_bd/

# Standard Vivado artefacts, so a GUI-created project is covered too.
# NOTE: *.tcl is deliberately NOT listed -- fpga/build_bd.tcl is source, and
# ignoring it would be the single most damaging entry in this file.
*.cache/
*.hw/
*.runs/
*.sim/
*.gen/
*.ip_user_files/
.Xil/
*.str
*.jou
*.backup.journal
*.pb
*.wdb
*.dcp
*.ltx
# Precise, so it does not catch the vendored r22sdf-master/sim/**/vsim.log
# files that are legitimately tracked.
vivado*.log

# Bitstreams and hardware platforms: build outputs, and large.
/ofdm_bd/*.xpr
*.bit
*.xsa
*.hwh

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# macOS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store